# Cursor Cloud specific instructions

These notes apply only to Cursor Cloud agents. Product rules stay in `AGENTS.md` and
`CONTRIBUTING.md`. Keep this file out of pull requests to `pingdotgg/t3code`.

## Toolchain

`package.json` pins the Node version (`engines.node`, currently 26.12.1) and pnpm
(`packageManager`, currently 12.14.0). Vite+ (`vp`) installs that Node. The environment install
runs `https://vite.plus` with `CI=1` and `VP_NODE_MANAGER=yes` when `vp` is missing, then
`vp i --frozen-lockfile -- --yes`. Login shells load `~/.config/vite-plus/env`.

- `/exec-daemon/node` is older than `engines.node` and wins on `PATH` in non-login shells. Run
  `vp`, `node`, and package scripts in a login shell (`bash -lc '...'`).
- `vp check` formats and lints. Markdown edits, including these rules, must be formatter-clean.
- `~/.gitconfig` rewrites GitHub remotes through `url.*.insteadof`. Server tests that compare
  remote URLs then see the rewritten URL. Run those tests with a `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL` that has no
  `url` section. Leave the managed rewrite in place for `git push`.

## Running the web app

- `vp run dev` from the repo root starts the server and the web app. Read ports from the
  `[dev-runner]` line. The preferred bases are web `5733` and server `13773`; a taken port shifts
  to the next free pair. `vp run dev:server` and `vp run dev:web` start one side.
- Leave `VITE_HTTP_URL` and `VITE_WS_URL` unset. Dev is single-origin and Vite proxies `/api`,
  `/ws`, `/oauth`, and `/.well-known`.
- Open the pairing URL the dev runner prints. The bare origin does not authenticate a new browser.
- The main checkout stores dev state in `~/.t3/dev`. A linked worktree uses its own `.t3`. Never
  point a dev server at the live `~/.t3/userdata`.
- `vp run dev` registers `Replay (dev)`, a local provider that plays recorded turns without a paid
  model. External provider CLIs are optional and are probed on `PATH`.

## Mobile

Follow `apps/mobile/README.md`. This environment does not install the Android SDK or JDK 17.
Native mobile CI runs on macOS (`apps/mobile/Brewfile`).

## Known flaky tests

- `apps/server/src/git/GitManager.test.ts` (cross-repo PR metadata, can time out at 12s).
- `apps/server/src/provider/ProviderRegistry.test.ts` (codex binaryPath re-probe ordering).
